# Mixed Arabic + English layout (RTL)

When a reply includes Arabic:

1. Treat Arabic as **RTL**. Wrap each Arabic block so clients render right-to-left, e.g.:

```html
<div dir="rtl">

الجملة العربية هنا.

</div>
```

2. Put the **Arabic** (RTL) on its own line / block.
3. Put related **English** on the **next line** (LTR as normal).
4. Continue alternating that way — do not glue Arabic and English on the same line when both are needed for clarity.

Examples of what belongs on the English line: file paths, class names, commands, error messages, Figma node ids, short technical terms kept in English by project convention.

Do **not** apply RTL wrapping to pure-English code blocks, file paths, or citations where it would break markdown/links.

Prefer:

```html
<div dir="rtl">

افتح الملف التالي.

</div>
```

```
MainShellScreen.kt
```

Over inline mixing like `افتح MainShellScreen.kt`.
